this camp for displaced people in  northern cameroon houses tens of  thousands of refugees many of them come  from the central african republic now  300 people are being repatriated hoping  to pick up where they left off or hoping  to start over  it's been eight years since i fled the  conflict to cameroon i came with my  husband and grandmother i'm not afraid  to go back because my neighbor who was  here with me has already left she helps  me a lot i just want to go back guardio  camp was set up in 2014 to accommodate  10 000 central africans fleeing fighting  between the government and seleka rebels  as the conflict intensified it's grown  and now hosts more than 10 times that  number  funding shortfalls as well as limited  humanitarian assistance and access to  basic services has led to deteriorating  conditions in the camp  when we first arrived i was happy in  cameroon but things got bad because of  the hospital and lack of food  to eat you're jostled by other people  from left to right and that's what's  pushing me to go home  hundreds of people have been repatriated  since the u.n backed process began in  2019 however the organization says the  decision is ultimately up to the  refugees themselves  repatriation is done on a voluntary  basis it is the first of all elements  that must be taken into consideration  and we unhcr give refugees the mapping  of safe areas in car and it is the  refugees who opt for return we do not  promote repatriation we facilitate that  is to say the refugee is aware of the  decision and we help him to return to  his country  the conflict in the central african  republic is not over and the  humanitarian situation is dire the world  food program estimates more than half of  the population of 5 million people don't  know where their next meal will come  from  and while many of these refugees say all  they remember of the villages they left  behind is death and devastation they'd  rather rebuild what's been destroyed in  their home country rather than live in  limbo elsewhere hippomorgan al jazeera
 

